(7087194, 1078284, 135744, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Neat:</b></div><hr/><i> i thought this was you, it was your type of noise! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Well spotted. Probably my favourite Topaz Adjust preset. I really must purchase the Nik software and try and expand my processing:)<br/> <br/>Btw congrats on the super result for you.</td>', 'Originally posted by Neat: i thought this was you, it was your type of noise!   Well spotted. Probably my favourite Topaz Adjust preset. I really must purchase the Nik software and try and expand my processing:) Btw congrats on the super result for you.', '2013-08-14 06:56:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(7087195, 1078284, 135744, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Cory:</b></div><hr/><i> You''ve pulled the shadows too hard here.  I see what you were going for, but there are two ways to deal with this.<br/> <br/>The first, is a massive hit of noise reduction, the other is to embrace the grain, and convert to black and white, while adding a bit more to even things out.<br/> <br/>Great image for Peter, and really a powerful image as well, very spooky cloud mass there! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks Cory - I do think on reflection there is too much noise. My laptop where I tend to do my processing tends not to make the noise so noticeable or perhaps it is the bottle of wine I have consumed whilst processing:)<br/> <br/>I think adding more noise may have been a wise move to make it look less like it was not meant to be there. It was a wild night and unfortunately I was in a tent:)<br/> <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by Cory: You''ve pulled the shadows too hard here.  I see what you were going for, but there are two ways to deal with this. The first, is a massive hit of noise reduction, the other is to embrace the grain, and convert to black and white, while adding a bit more to even things out. Great image for Peter, and really a powerful image as well, very spooky cloud mass there!   Thanks Cory - I do think on reflection there is too much noise. My laptop where I tend to do my processing tends not to make the noise so noticeable or perhaps it is the bottle of wine I have consumed whilst processing:) I think adding more noise may have been a wise move to make it look less like it was not meant to be there. It was a wild night and unfortunately I was in a tent:) ', '2013-08-14 07:00:52.000000', NULL, 0),
